{"term":"secrete","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:783c4f082f3d24d312","definition":"Separated; discrete.","example":"[…] they ſuppoſing Two other Divine Hypoſtaſes Superiour thereunto, which were perfectly Secrete from Matter.\n[…]\nThis ſo containeth all things, as not being yet ſecrete and diſtinct; whereas in the Second they are diſcerned and diſtinguiſhed by Reaſon; that is, they are Actually diſtinguiſhed in their Ideas; whereas the Firſt is the Simple and Fecund Power of all things.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, obsolete, rare","register":"not-comparable, obsolete, rare","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secrete#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8da213e2998dc92c1a","definition":"To extract a substance from blood, sap, or similar to produce and emit waste for excretion or for the fulfilling of a physiological function.","example":"Why one set of cells should secrete bile, another urea, and so on, we do not know.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["secern"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"usually","register":"transitive, usually","wordFamily":["cosecreted","hypersecrete","hypersecreting","neurosecrete","nonsecreted","nonsecreting","oversecrete","resecrete","rhizosecrete","secretability","secretable","secretagogue","secretase","secretin","secretolysis","secretome","secretomotor","secretor","secretosome","unsecreted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secrete#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c906f5cbcf808a08cc","definition":"To exude or yield.","example":"If you won’t believe my great new doctrine (which, by the bye, is as old as the Greeks), that souls secrete their bodies, as snails do shells, you will remain in outer darkness.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["cosecreted","hypersecrete","hypersecreting","neurosecrete","nonsecreted","nonsecreting","oversecrete","resecrete","rhizosecrete","secretability","secretable","secretagogue","secretase","secretin","secretolysis","secretome","secretomotor","secretor","secretosome","unsecreted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secrete#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0b0680ff3f99a7662e","definition":"To conceal.","example":"With those words the passenger opened the coach-door and got in; not at all assisted by his fellow-passengers, who had expeditiously secreted their watches and purses in their boots, and were now making a general pretence of being asleep.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cosecreted","hypersecrete","hypersecreting","neurosecrete","nonsecreted","nonsecreting","oversecrete","resecrete","rhizosecrete","secretability","secretable","secretagogue","secretase","secretin","secretolysis","secretome","secretomotor","secretor","secretosome","unsecreted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secrete#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8915042e3222fdd6d4","definition":"Archaic form of secret.","example":"a secrete breach, a secrete bed (Spenser)","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"alt-of, archaic","register":"alt-of, archaic","wordFamily":["cosecreted","hypersecrete","hypersecreting","neurosecrete","nonsecreted","nonsecreting","oversecrete","resecrete","rhizosecrete","secretability","secretable","secretagogue","secretase","secretin","secretolysis","secretome","secretomotor","secretor","secretosome","unsecreted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikk